      "side": 1,
      "message": "For 1:\n\nWe can separate the original logic to 2 section\n\n1. Load the file paths from $(DEVICE_PRODUCT_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE) to inputPaths in `line#186`. And if there\u0027s no input path, I will treat it as below ifndef condition which will add a flag between `line#225 to line#228` and do the related logic on `line#270` for generate the `include $(BUILD_PHONY_PACKAGE)`.\n```\nifndef DEVICE_PRODUCT_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE\n  my_framework_matrix_deps :\u003d\n  include $(BUILD_PHONY_PACKAGE)\n```\n2. This is the main logic if having `$(DEVICE_PRODUCT_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE)` defined which can be map to line#182, \n```\nelse # DEVICE_PRODUCT_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE\n  ...\n  ...\n\n  # DEVICE_PRODUCT_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE specifies absolute paths\n  LOCAL_GENERATED_SOURCES :\u003d $(DEVICE_PRODUCT_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE)\n  ...\n  ...\n  LOCAL_GEN_FILE_DEPENDENCIES +\u003d $(my_empty_manifest)\n  LOCAL_ASSEMBLE_VINTF_FLAGS +\u003d -c \"$(my_empty_manifest)\"\n\n  include $(BUILD_FRAMEWORK_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX)\nendif # DEVICE_PRODUCT_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE\n```\n\n\nFor 2:\nIt is actually the section for `line#37\u0027s` Command part, but didn\u0027t handle `$(PRIVATE_ADDITIONAL_ENV_VARS)` because it is come from `$(GEN): PRIVATE_ADDITIONAL_ENV_VARS :\u003d $(LOCAL_ASSEMBLE_VINTF_ENV_VARS_OVERRIDE)`\nin [hardware/interfaces/compatibility_matrices/compatibility_matrix.mk](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:hardware/interfaces/compatibility_matrices/compatibility_matrix.mk;l\u003d103;bpv\u003d0) and it is not being used in this 2 cases.\n\nBut for `foreach varname,$(PRIVATE_ENV_VARS),$(varname)\u003d\"$($(varname))\")` it is already handled by ${assembleVintfEnv} and it being used for `framework_compatibility_matrix.device.xml`.",
